    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L03-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "3.3: Let’s Make Some Curves",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Since graphs of polynomials can curve up and down multiple times, they can have points that are higher or lower than the rest of the points around them. These points are relative maximums and relative minimums. In the second graph, there…",
